{title: Abide with Me}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]A[**]bide with [**]me: [**]fast [F]falls the [G]even[C]tide; [**]
[C]The [G]darkness [F]dee[C]pens; [Dm]Lord, with [C]me a[G]bide: [**]
[C]When [G]other [C]hel[**]pers [F]fail, and [A]comforts [Dm]flee, [**]
[G]Help [C]of the [Am]helpless, [F]O a[C]bide [G]with [C]me. [**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Swift [**]to its [**]close [**]ebbs [F]out life's [G]little [C]day; [**]
[C]Earth's [G]joys grow [F]dim, [C]its [Dm]glories [C]pass a[G]way, [**]
[C]Change [G]and de[C]cay [**]in [F]all a[A]round I [Dm]see; [**]
[G]O [C]Thou who [Am]changest [F]not, a[C]bide [G]with [C]me. [**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C]I [**]need Thy [**]pre[**]sence [F]every [G]passing [C]hour; [**]
[C]What [G]but Thy [F]grace [C]can [Dm]foil the [C]tempter's [G]pow[**]er?
[C]Who, [G]like Thy[C]self, [**]my [F]guide and [A]stay can [Dm]be? [**]
[G]Through [C]cloud and [Am]sunshine, [F]Lord, a[C]bide [G]with [C]me. [**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C]I [**]fear no [**]foe, [**]with [F]Thee at [G]hand to [C]bless: [**]
[C]Ills [G]have no [F]weight, [C]and [Dm]tears no [C]bitter[G]ness. [**]
[C]Where [G]is death's [C]sting? [**]where, [F]grave, thy [A]victo[Dm]ry? [**]
[G]I [C]triumph [Am]still, if [F]Thou a[C]bide [G]with [C]me. [**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 5}
[C]Hold [**]Thou Thy [**]Cross [**]be[F]fore my [G]closing [C]eyes: [**]
[C]Shine [G]through the [F]gloom, [C]and [Dm]point me [C]to the [G]skies: [**]
[C]Heaven's [G]morning [C]breaks, [**]and [F]earth's vain [A]shadows [Dm]flee: [**]
[G]In [C]life, in [Am]death, O [F]Lord, a[C]bide [G]with [C]me. [**]
{end_of_verse}
